      {
        "introduction": "God brings a fascinating vision to Ezekiel in demonstration of the new life which Israel will have. The visual image—of dry bones coming to life—must bring a smile to Ezekiel's face as he now relates the vision."
      },
      {
        "title": "",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "title": "Vision of Dry Bones",
            "references": [
              {
                "book": "Ezekiel",
                "chapter": 37,
                "verse": "1-14"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "introduction": "Another sign is to be shown to the people. Two sticks, one representing the northern tribes and the other depicting the tribe of Judah, are to be held together to signify the reunification of the nation of Israel. This is followed by a messianic prophecy of the new kingdom to come."
      },
      {
        "title": "",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "title": "Sign of Two Sticks",
            "references": [
              {
                "book": "Ezekiel",
